When you declare multiple body parameters using Pydantic models (such as `item` and `user`), FastAPI uses the parameter names as keys (field names) in the body [1]. 

Therefore, it will expect a JSON request body structured with those parameter names as the top-level keys, like this [1]:

```JSON
{
    "item": {
        "name": "Foo",
        "description": "The pretender",
        "price": 42.0,
        "tax": 3.2
    },
    "user": {
        "username": "dave",
        "full_name": "Dave Smith"
    }
}
```

When a function declares more than one body parameter as a Pydantic model (such as `item` and `user`), FastAPI uses the parameter names as keys in the JSON body [1]. 

For example, it expects a body like this:
```JSON
{
    "item": {
        "name": "Foo",
        "description": "The pretender",
        "price": 42.0,
        "tax": 3.2
    },
    "user": {
        "username": "dave",
        "full_name": "Dave Grohl"
    }
}
```

